      "accessed": "2026-11-14",
      "note": "The burgundy and orange cheatlines and the meatball; the scheme first came back on a Q400 (retired 2023)."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Embraer delivered N652MK in these colors on 18 November 2022 ('MK' for founder Milt Kuolt); the same retro scheme flew earlier on a Q400. Flown by Horizon (QXE). Drawn from Alaska's photo of the left side and checked on the right (2026-03-14): the stripes, titles and tail are the same both sides, 'HORIZON AIR' aft of 'Alaska' on both. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the March 2026 side-on photo of N652MK (right side; doors as the check: the forward door at x 0.115-0.135, the aft at 0.74-0.77 of the E175's length), drawn on the E175: the stripes had been drawn rising to the tail cone, as on a 737; on the E175 they run level in metres, just under the windows, crossing the aft door's lower half, and so fall as shares of the fuselage aft where the tail cone sweeps up, running off the belly at about x 0.93. Re-measured as smooth curves (the three bands about equal), their front ends square at the nose tip. 'Alaska' runs 0.106-0.28 (its end over the forward door) and 'HORIZON AIR' 0.288-0.383, about 1.2 m further forward than first drawn from Alaska's photo; 'Alaska' lowercase about 0.55 of its A.",
  "from": "2022-11",
